Type Filter
• Can supply arguments to the filter.
• Filter instances are created by using Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.
ObjectFactory.
• They're NOT created using DI (Dependency Injection).
• The lifetime of filter instances is by default transient (a new filter instance gets created every
time when it is invoked).
• But optionally, you can re-use the same instance of filter class across multiple requests, by
setting a property called TypeFilterAttribute.IsReusable to 'true'.
• Filter classes NEED NOT be registered (added) to the IoC container.
• Filter classes CAN inject services using both constructor injection or method injection.

